course: dictionary
lesson: 3941
title: Keeping your word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Fulfil» means to do what you promised, or to make something happen that was needed or wished for. «It is better not to make a vow than to make one and not fulfil it» is about making a serious promise. The clue is the word vow, so fulfil must mean keep or do what was promised.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «keep» or «do» in place of fulfil: «not to make a vow than to make one and not keep it» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. In the Ramayana, Rama goes into exile to keep his father's word, which is the same idea as fulfilling a promise.
explain: Fulfil can also mean to make a dream come true, or to meet a need. The spelling changes in American English: they write fulfill with two l's. Both spellings mean the same thing.
fact: «Fulfil» means to do what you promised or what is needed.
fact: «Fulfil» can mean to make a dream, wish or hope come true, as in «fulfil a dream».
fact: «Fulfil» can mean to meet a need or a requirement.
fact: «Fulfil» can mean to make someone feel happy and satisfied with what they do.
fact: In American English the spelling is fulfill, with two l's.
exercise: «It is better not to make a vow than to make one and not fulfil it» (Ecclesiastes 5:5). What does fulfil mean here? | To break a promise by mistake | Forget about it | *To do what was promised | To lose something you own
exercise: Which word in «Fulfil every commitment» means a promise? | every | Qur'an | Fulfil | *commitment
exercise: «When you make a vow to God, do not delay to fulfil it.» What does this tell you to do? | *Keep your promise to God without delay | Make another vow straight away | Ask someone else to fix it | Wait a year before you start
test: «She worked for years to fulfil her dream of running a bakery.» What does fulfil mean in this sentence? | To sleep through a dream | *To make a dream come true | To forget a dream | To tell a dream to others
test: «The new bridge will fulfil a need in the town.» Which meaning fits best? | *To meet a need | To break a bridge | To ask the council for money | To paint a bridge
exam: Which sentence uses fulfil to mean keep a promise? | Dad will fulfil the table with books | The bird will fulfil its nest by spring | The sky will fulfil with rain at noon | *Ella will fulfil her promise to help Sam tomorrow
